[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one bug and closed on 5 October. It held three
problems. Engineering fixed the parser and retired booking-v3's form. Nothing has touched the
third: the five dates that move by one day.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, and one of its problems is still open: the date moves by one day (day-shift).
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

### `parser`: the shared parser read every date month first · fixed

A day-first tenant books 7 April (`07/04`); the invite says 4 July. Day and month swap, on every
channel except booking-v3's form. Fixed by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.

### `hint`: booking-v3's form told people to type the month first · won't fix

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants on that form (Alder Physio,
Copper Studio, Pale Harbour) typed what the hint said, and the form read it day first. Same flip
for the reporter, different code: the parser fix does not touch it. Won't fix: the form is retired.

### `day-shift`: the date moves by one day, nothing is flipped · open

"Tuesday 12 May" on the invite, "Monday 11 May" in the calendar. One meeting on Tuesday in Lisbon
and Monday in Toronto. An invite that arrives before its booking. The desk noted these five as a
one-day move and filed them under `parser` by tenant, so they were closed with it. A swap of day
and month cannot move a date by one day, so the parser fix cannot close them. This looks like a
time zone conversion at midnight (not confirmed in the code).

## How to tell them apart

- Day and month swapped, booked through booking-v3's form at a day-first tenant: `hint`.
- Day and month swapped, any other way in: `parser`.
- Off by one day, no swap: `day-shift`.

Subject lines do not tell them apart: all three arrive as "Date is wrong". Intake's tag does not
either: it guesses from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant's form.

## What changes for the desk

- A new one-day report goes to [#3](https://github.com/MatthieuVeillon/mega-s01e03/issues/3), not
  to #4471.
- Merging on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put all three
  into one ticket. A new decision record should replace 0001, not an edit.

